# local/extio.tcl -- rig-local extio configuration
#
# Sourced at the END of config/extioconf.tcl, after discovery and wiring are
# set up. Absent file = all defaults. An error in this file aborts only the
# extio subprocess's config (see local/README for what that costs and how to
# spot it).

# ---- obs-leader auto-bind consent ------------------------------------------
# MOVED: this declaration now lives in local/rig.tcl with the other declared
# rig facts, as
#
#     setting extio obs_autobind auto
#
# The value is a NAME FILTER, *not* a boolean: off (default) / auto (bind
# whatever single box announces obs_leader) / <boxname> (only that box).
# Boolean spellings (1/on/true) normalize to auto. A runtime
# `send extio {extio_obs_autobind auto}` persists straight into rig.tcl —
# a set IS the declaration now. A legacy extio_obs_autobind line in THIS
# file still works (it persists any changed value into rig.tcl at boot),
# but rig.tcl is the one place to look.

# ---- other rig-local extio overrides ---------------------------------------
# Port pinning, extra forwards, etc. This file runs inside the extio
# subprocess interp with all of extioconf.tcl's procs available.
